(
========================================================================
 PUZZLESCRIPT RULE-ENGINE TUTORIAL
 Paste this whole file into the editor at puzzlescript.net and hit RUN.
 Written for classic PuzzleScript (not the "Next" fork). Most objects
 are flat colors; a few that sit ON TOP of another object use a small
 centered sprite instead of a full block, so whatever's underneath
 still shows around the edges.
========================================================================

 TUTORIAL MAP -- Ctrl+F for a tag like [T3] to jump straight to it.
 Nothing below [T0] is conceptually new - it's just the required
 boilerplate every PuzzleScript file needs. Skip straight to [T1]
 if you want to get to the interesting part immediately.

 [T0]  Objects / Legend / Sounds / CollisionLayers - boilerplate, skim it
 [T1]  One pass, top to bottom: how a turn actually executes
 [T2]  A single rule already loops itself to exhaustion
 [T3]  Rule GROUPS: + and STARTLOOP/ENDLOOP, for rules that need
       to feed each other
 [T4]  Direction keywords: explicit vs "no direction = all four",
       plus the horizontal/vertical shortcut
 [T5]  "or" properties vs "and" aggregates
 [T6]  Removal rule: only things referred to (then dropped) get deleted
 [T7]  Collision layers: what can share a cell, what can't
 [T8]  again: self-driving multi-turn animation
 [T9]  late: rules that run after movement resolves
 [T10] Grab bag: DEBUG flag, the NO keyword, object identity
 [T11] Capping how far a self-looping spread goes (a generic version
       of the Wood -> Spark -> Flame / Explosion:C -> B -> A pattern)

 Every tag above appears twice more below: once as a comment right
 above the RULES it describes, and once right above the LEVEL that
 demonstrates it. Each of those comments ends with "-- next: [Tn]"
 so you can just keep searching forward. There's also a corresponding
 in-game MESSAGE after every level recapping the point.
========================================================================
)

